    "findings": [
      "imp_cases uses ded3 over G=[a->b,b->c,not-a->c]. The true branch has a::G and applies h1 then h2; the false branch uses h2.weaken from G for not-a->c and the new head not-a. Existing Kalmar.cases_on discharges precisely those two branches using the same object-calculus hC; it adds no Lean Classical axiom.",
      "occurs_lt_top follows from the existing not_occurs_of_top_le: an occurrence refutes top f<=n, then Nat.lt_of_not_ge gives n<top f. Pinned Lean4.32 source defines that Nat lemma via the constructive decidable-order alternative, not global excluded middle.",
      "update_comm moves unchanged from the unsectioned universe-u/V semantics block of TarskiClean to the matching semantics block of TarskiCalculus. Namespace, universe, implicit V, binder names/order and proof remain exact. TarskiClean transitively imports TarskiCalculus through Leibniz/Derived, so old import paths still expose the same declaration.",
      "rho4 uses update_comm at i,j,di,dj in the correct reversed orientation to match h di dj. The i=j branch remains. rho1 chooses e j; both indices evaluate to e j, so simp can erase the explicit equality split.",
      "All nonproof definitions, inductives, Rows/instance fields, imports, options and section inclusion policies remain unchanged. The only visibility change is earlier availability of the existing update_comm."
    ]
  },
