    "findings": [
      "The universal branch first transports the ambient wfForm guard by sat_guard, then applies the induction hypothesis at scons <x,hx> env under the explicit WF proof binder. Subtype.forall.symm converts exactly forall ambient x, forall hx:WF x into forall x:Domain. liftEnv_scons rewrites the same environment as before.",
      "The existential branch transports the guard, converts WF x and rawSat into exists hx:WF x, rawSat using exists_prop.symm, then applies the induction hypothesis at that subtype witness. Subtype.exists.symm reconstructs the single Domain witness. No representative choice or inhabited-domain premise is inserted.",
      "Atomic subtype equality and pair/successor disjunctions use Subtype.ext_iff.symm in the correct value-equality-to-subtype-equality direction. The ambient membership relation remains definitionally domainMem on subtype values.",
      "domain_separation reuses sat_translate_scons at the same slot0 tested element. domain_replacement replaces exactly four occurrences of the private raw_rel_iff by existing sat_translate_relOf; its relOf left side unfolds to the identical Sat at output0,input1.",
      "replacementForm and replacementForm_spec are byte-exact, including both WF guards. The raw global functionality proof still extracts WF for input/output before applying the original global subtype Functional assumption; both image directions and output WF closure keep their original domain guards and witnesses.",
      "The removed private helper has no external selected source/client or report use and is definitionally the existing public transport, so deletion eliminates a duplicate environment proof. All25 retained public declaration headers, five nonproof definitions and all imports remain exact."
    ]
  },
